From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M. Samil Atesoglu <samil.atesoglu@nodos.dev>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0300
Subject: Fix pages freezing under virtual time while they wait for the clock

Virtual time stands still while a task runs. A page that waits for
performance.now() or Date.now() to change, as pages that measure the
clock's resolution do, loops forever: its task never ends, so the virtual
time budget is never spent and no frame is drawn again.

While time is overridden, the clock page script reads moves on by a
microsecond for each reading that would not be later than the last, as
time passes while script runs in a browser. Virtual time itself, and so
timers and frame times, is unaffected; script's clock goes back to
reading it once virtual time passes the readings.

